umN8Vd7OA38qthdyGPYvZW3MLVoLm/w\nvI2H0tWbmNGvBjAKCo6Oy/6dOdmONZ7AFrCVc7BOZvtO/jPqvuKPsj4tiRUb\n+VyYO+Go82H6rQHaleP8vV3YTzw85pYlKf/3ZpHBOVRZ3Dlx7iGDKb6V3zep\ngQjSDJcFvXx9HH31YyDK+XFZfNqIUi4/RdUg1mF5InN4JDHzN+PL50/mH6/T\nTax4x8GzAJx7vTOZHFGaVbP/WHUnKeZkdy3Mbg==\n",
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "### Build an Undo History Stack\r\n\r\nThe Undo button needs to remember **two** things at every step: the list of filtered products AND the list of active filter pills.\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n**Do This:**\r\n\r\n1. Inside the `applyFilter` function, copy your data before filtering:\r\n\r\n      - Create an empty array `itemsCopy` and use a `for` loop to push every item from `currentProducts` into it.\r\n      - Create an empty array `pillsCopy` and use a `for` loop to push every item from `activeFilters` into it.\r\n\r\n\r\n2.  Still inside `applyFilter`, after your loops, save the history:\r\n\r\n      - Create a state object containing your copies: `{ items: itemsCopy, pills: pillsCopy }`.\r\n      - Push this object onto the `historyStack`.\r\n\r\n3. Inside the `undoBtn` event listener, implement the undo button:\r\n\r\n      - **Check for history:** If `historyStack.length` is greater than 0, proceed.\r\n      - **Restore state:** Pop the last object from `historyStack`.\r\n          - Set `currentProducts` to `lastState.items`.\r\n          - Set `activeFilters` to `lastState.pills`.\r\n      - **Update display:** Call `updateUI()` to show the old state.\r\n\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>Need help? Ask our AI assistant...</summary>\r\n\r\n**Example Prompts:**\r\n\r\n  - \"How do I use a for loop to copy one array into another?\"\r\n  - \"Why do I need to copy the arrays before pushing them to the stack?\"\r\n  - \"How do I access the `items` property from the object I popped off the stack?\"\r\n  - \"My Undo button works, but the filter pills aren't disappearing. What did I miss?\"\r\n\r\n</details\\>",
    "submittable": "false",
    "disable_edit_run_for_submission": "false",
    "hide_share_and_remix": "false",
    "widget_view": "false",
    "initial_view_mode": "split",
    "ai_tutor_mode": "engineer",
    "predict_settings": {
